-- title:
--   Descent to K of integrality over K[jmatĥ⁻¹]
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, let $\sigma\colon K\to\mathbb{C}$ be a ring homomorphism, let $N\ge 1$, let $m$ be a natural number, let $f$ be a modular form of weight $2m$ for $\Gamma_0(N)$, and let $y$ be a Laurent series over $K$ (an element of `LaurentSeries K`). Write $\hat\jmath_L=$ `coeffEmb L jq` for the image in `LaurentSeries L` of $jq=q^{-1}\cdot(\text{the rational power series }jNumQ)$ under the coefficientwise map induced by $\mathbb{Q}\to L$, and $\theta=$ `thetaL` for the operator $g\mapsto q\,\mathrm{d}g/\mathrm{d}q$ on Laurent series. Assume that applying $\sigma$ to the coefficients of $y$ and multiplying by $(\theta\hat\jmath_{\mathbb{C}})^m$ gives the Laurent series attached to the $q$-expansion `qExpansion 1 f` of $f$ of width $1$. The conclusion is that $$y^2\,\hat\jmath_K^{\,m}\,(\hat\jmath_K-1728)^m$$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra `Algebra.adjoin K {(coeffEmb K jq)⁻¹}` of `LaurentSeries K` generated by $\hat\jmath_K^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the descent to a general $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra field $K$ of the integrality statement, over the ring generated by the inverse $q$-expansion of the modular invariant, attached to a weight-$2m$ form on $\Gamma_0(N)$ whose $q$-expansion factors as $y\cdot(\theta\hat\jmath)^m$; the hypothesis is imposed after transport of $y$ to $\mathbb{C}$ along $\sigma$, while the conclusion lives in $K((q))$. It feeds the construction of mod-$p$ forms and cusp forms from $q$-expansions, being used by [`ModPForms.exists_isModPFormFn_qexpOfWeight_eq_of_mem_modPMod`](thm.html#ModPForms.exists_isModPFormFn_qexpOfWeight_eq_of_mem_modPMod) and [`ModPForms.exists_isModPCuspFormFn_qexpOfWeight_eq_of_mem_modPCusp`](thm.html#ModPForms.exists_isModPCuspFormFn_qexpOfWeight_eq_of_mem_modPCusp).
-- source:
